{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having abdominal pain and vomiting. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. I started vomiting bile last night—no blood—and the pain got worse. It feels just like my past bowel blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You have a history of sclerosing mesenteritis and recurrent obstructions. Did you try anything at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I took extra Phenergan and morphine, but it didn’t help. I still passed gas, though, so I wasn’t completely blocked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good you’re still passing gas. We did a CT scan and a plain X-ray. The CT shows your duodenum is more dilated than before, suggesting a partial blockage, but contrast is moving through."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a full blockage? But it feels just like the last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely a partial or transient obstruction, related to your mesenteritis. We’ll keep you NPO for now, give IV fluids, and vent your stomach through the G-tube to relieve pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my warfarin? My INR was 5.0 in the ER—that’s high, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2182-06-14 23:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s elevated. We’re holding your warfarin for now in case we need any procedures. We’ll restart it when you’re more stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2182-06-15 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show mild dehydration and low potassium. We’re correcting that with IV fluids and supplements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2182-06-15 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ve been feeling a bit weak. Is the fatty liver on the CT related to my hepatitis C?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2182-06-15 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely. But your liver enzymes are stable, and ammonia is normal, so it’s not causing your current symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2182-06-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better—bowel sounds are returning. We’re going to start clear liquids slowly and cap your G-tube to see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2182-06-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Can I go back on my regular meds soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2182-06-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re restarting your metoclopramide and misoprostol to help gut motility. Aciphex isn’t available here, so we’re using famotidine for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2182-06-17 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been tolerating liquids well. We’re advancing to a soft diet today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2182-06-17 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried about not eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2182-06-18 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We scheduled a small bowel follow-through to check your motility. It’s a test where you drink contrast, and we watch it move through your intestines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2182-06-18 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it make me nauseous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2182-06-18 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give anti-nausea meds beforehand. It’s important to see if your bowels are moving properly despite the structural changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2182-06-21 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—the SBFT showed normal motility. The contrast reached the colon in 50 minutes, which is normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2182-06-21 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why do I keep getting these blockage-like episodes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2182-06-21 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your anatomy is altered from mesenteritis—dilated loops, tethering—but the function is okay. It’s likely transient partial obstructions due to inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2182-06-22 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re going to try restarting your home medications fully, including Lyrica and Lamictal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2182-06-22 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been so tired and a bit confused since yesterday. Could that be from the meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2182-06-22 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We checked your liver and ammonia—both normal. We think the altered mental status is from restarting Lyrica and Lamictal at full dose too quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2182-06-22 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to hold Lyrica for now and reduce Lamictal to 25mg. We’ll increase slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2182-06-22 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ve been anxious and having trouble sleeping too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2182-06-22 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue trazodone and lorazepam as needed. Social work will also check in to support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2182-06-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting TPN today. Nutrition feels it’s needed because you’re not meeting your needs by mouth, especially after the setback."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2182-06-23 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was hoping to avoid TPN. I’ve had complications before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2182-06-23 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But with your malnutrition and risk of further obstruction, TPN will help you heal and maintain strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2182-06-24 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re stable. We’re continuing TPN and your oral diet. We’ll keep monitoring your G-tube output."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2182-06-25 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m having more pain again, and I vomited. My G-tube just drained over 1300cc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2182-06-25 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry. We’re going back to NPO and IV fluids. A new X-ray shows ileus, not a full obstruction. It should resolve with rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2182-06-25 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is this going to keep happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2182-06-25 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s frustrating, I know. Your underlying condition makes you prone to these episodes. We’re adjusting your pain plan to avoid heavy IV opioids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2182-06-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ileus is improving. We’re restarting oral meds and will try clears again soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2182-06-27 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Another X-ray shows diffuse bowel distention—likely ileus again. We’ll hold oral intake for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2182-06-27 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so tired of being stuck in bed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2182-06-27 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s hard. But your body needs time. We’re continuing TPN and will try liquids again when you stabilize."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2182-06-28 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The distention is improving. We’re seeing better motility. We’ll try small sips of water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2182-06-29 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. We’re advancing diet slowly. We’ve restarted warfarin at your home dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2182-06-29 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my Lyrica and Lamictal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2182-06-29 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve restarted Lyrica at a lower dose—75mg twice daily—and increased Lamictal to 50mg. We’ll keep titrating up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2182-06-30 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "X-ray shows moderate fecal loading but no obstruction. We’re adding bisacodyl to help with bowel movements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2182-06-30 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been constipated. Should I take more senna?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2182-06-30 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching to bisacodyl for now. We’ll adjust as needed. Docusate will stay for softening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2182-07-01 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re stable. We’re continuing TPN at home. Your gastroenterologist will follow up on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2182-07-01 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous about going home on TPN. What if I have another flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2182-07-01 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you clear instructions. If vomiting or severe pain returns, come back. Otherwise, keep your GI follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2182-07-02 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning discharge tomorrow. You’re on oral pain meds—morphine SR and liquid as needed—and tizanidine for muscle spasms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2182-07-02 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I still need the G-tube venting at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2182-07-02 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Only if you feel bloated or nauseous. Otherwise, keep it capped. Use Phenergan as needed for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2182-07-02 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my dry eyes from Sjogren’s?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2182-07-02 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re sending artificial tears. Pilocarpine isn’t available here, but your regular doctor can restart it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2182-07-03 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re being discharged today. Your vitals are stable, and you’re managing symptoms well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2182-07-03 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. It’s been a long stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2182-07-03 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you had a setback, but you’ve recovered. Continue TPN, all meds, and follow up with your PCP and GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2182-07-03 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I just hope I can avoid another hospitalization."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2182-07-03 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We all do. But now you know the signs. Don’t hesitate to reach out if things worsen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2182-07-03 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate everything you’ve done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2182-07-03 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve worked hard too. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2182-06-14 22:59:00",
    "admission_end": "2182-07-03 13:57:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with a history of sclerosing mesenteritis, chronic pain, and hepatitis C, was admitted for abdominal pain and vomiting consistent with prior partial small bowel obstructions. Imaging showed duodenal dilation suggestive of partial obstruction, and she was managed with NPO status, G-tube venting, IV fluids, and pain control. She initially improved but had a relapse with severe pain and high G-tube output, leading to a diagnosis of ileus. TPN was initiated due to malnutrition and inability to maintain oral intake. Altered mental status occurred upon restarting home neuropsychiatric medications, which resolved with dose adjustments. She was gradually transitioned back to oral intake and medications, including morphine, metoclopramide, and misoprostol. Warfarin was held and restarted as INR normalized. She was discharged home on TPN, with stable symptoms and a plan for outpatient follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Chronic hepatitis C without mention of hepatic coma",
      "Malnutrition of moderate degree",
      "Dehydration",
      "Sicca syndrome",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Paralytic ileus",
      "Altered mental status",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
